L","user":{"login":"Ivorforce","id":2308167,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIzMDgxNjc=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2308167?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce","html_url":"https://github.com/Ivorforce","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-01-03T14:49:35Z","updated_at":"2025-01-03T16:49:13Z","body":"> Does this produce the same assembly when compiled? \r\n\r\nYes.\r\n\r\n> Is there a performance impact?\r\n\r\nNo.\r\n\r\nInlining is pretty much guaranteed through 3 factors: It's declared on a class, it's a template function, and each specialization has only one caller. \r\nI'm confident enough in this that I normally wouldn't test this explicitly. But it's a convenient opportunity to challenge my assumptions, so I made one anyway: https://godbolt.org/z/TqToveMqh\r\nBoth the code and the assembly are a bit difficult to read since it's a constructed demo, but it should be analogous to the Godot source. \r\nAnd yes - I'm happy to report both functions are equivalent!","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2569346187/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":